      "notes": "Just the daube today (roast moved to Wednesday). INSTANT POT: brown the beef in batches, soften onion/garlic/carrots (6, thick), add tomato paste, tomatoes, orange zest, cloves, star anise, herbes de Provence, bay; deglaze with 1 1/2 cups red wine + 1/2 cup water; HIGH 45 min + 15 min natural release. Olives in, Sauté to thicken if thin, skim fat. Carb is the sourdough. Serves 8: Sun dinner for two, his Mon dinner, Tue/Wed lunches, ~3 to freeze (2 for Sat 11/21). Tonight's carb is the sourdough. For the leftover portions (Mon dinner, Tue/Wed lunches, freezer), make garlic smashed baby reds while the pot runs: 1 lb skin-on boiled with 3 garlic cloves, smashed with 1 tbsp butter + 1 tbsp olive oil, a small pinch of salt, pepper and some cooking water. They freeze fine next to the daube."
